  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Srini",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5526995d3be3953ef37bb6a504637521778736720d30c79090668f8ffbb0ce02",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5526995d3be3-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Srini, the United States argues that the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA) includes its own remedial scheme, which supports the petitioner\u2019s position."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Jacobs",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5526995d3be3953ef37bb6a504637521778736720d30c79090668f8ffbb0ce02",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5526995d3be3-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Jacobs, the government is one of the two largest issuers of credit\u2011card receipts, so excluding it from FCRA protections would be contrary to public interest."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Jacobs",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5526995d3be3953ef37bb6a504637521778736720d30c79090668f8ffbb0ce02",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5526995d3be3-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Jacobs, the 1996 amendment to the FCRA that changed \u201ccredit reporting agency\u201d to \u201cperson\u201d was a deliberate step, indicating congressional intent to include entities like the government."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5526995d3be3953ef37bb6a504637521778736720d30c79090668f8ffbb0ce02",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5526995d3be3-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The consequences of the Court\u2019s ruling could be enormous for the Federal Treasury."
      }
    ],
